infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same problem, two architectures, different prices
  desc Team A split into 15 microservices; Team B kept a monolith with clean module boundaries — one B2B order/billing platform, two prices
  compares
    - label Team A
      children
        - label 15 microservices
          desc Codebase split into fifteen independently deployable services
        - label Deploys: fast, independent
          desc Each service ships on its own — high deployability
        - label Billing scales on its own
          desc The billing component scales independently of the rest
        - label Debug billing: 40 minutes
          desc One discrepancy traces through 6 services + 3 message queues
        - label Coupling moves to infrastructure
          desc Service contracts, version management, distributed failures
    - label Team B
      children
        - label Monolith + module boundaries
          desc One deployable unit with clean internal module seams
        - label Deploys: whole app at once
          desc Cannot ship the billing engine independently
        - label Billing cannot scale alone
          desc No independent scaling of the billing component
        - label Debug billing: 10 minutes
          desc A single stack trace, no distributed trace to read
        - label Coupling stays in code
          desc The module boundaries hold it in place
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
